# Code style

- Simple first. If a solution looks complex, simplify it before proposing it. Reject overkill.
- Avoid magic numbers and hardcoded values.
- Naming matters. Vague names are a smell; `helper` in a name is a smell.
- Keep the diff easy to review: no unrelated changes. Put new private methods at the bottom of the file.
- Reuse patterns already in the codebase instead of inventing new ones.
